n  nations and this calls for our most  gentle prayers and fierce advocacy  remembering that we are united with  those we who with whom we do not yet  know or understand  and this calls for more patience than we  normally bring with us to church but God  has made us worthy of this calling to  which we have been called a calling to  be united with Christ and other  Christians and by God's grace and the  power of the Holy Spirit and through the  taste of breads from around the world  and a drink from the cup of blessing we  have a foretaste of what that unity  might look like a unity that says all  are welcome a unity that with the  prophet Isaiah calls us to beat our  swords into plowshares our spears into  pruning hooks a unity that is so  desperately needed in the world and each  of our lives so I hope you'll join me in  praying that this may be so amen

